 In conclusion,
 UseEffect is a hook.At the end of day,Hook is  a function.How can you call that function?You called the useEffect function by giving two parameters.One is call back function and other one is dependency array.Without dependency array,useEffect will call the callback function after every render.This approach is bad thats why we use dependency array.If passed empty dependency,it will call only once after first time render.
 
 Now if i want that ,whenever my search text is updating,useEffect callback function should be called.For this, passed the search text in its dependency array
 
 useEffect(()=>{
    console.log('useEffect call');
    
   },[searchText])  //this array is known as dependency array
   
  Remember,
 => Useeffect  will always called after render,not before render.
 => Useeffect callback function will allways called on below scenarios
  
 a) without dependency array[]===>once after initial render+  everytime after render
 b) empty dependency array[]===> once after initial render
 c) with dependent data [searchText]===> once after initial render+  everytime after render when searchText updates
