Diff btw useLayoutEffect vs useEffect

useLayoutEffect runs scyronously after a render before the screen is updated while useEffect runs ascyronously after render after the ui is updated

useLayoutEffect:
Render → useLayoutEffect runs → UI Updates → User sees screen
         ↑                       
    (Changes happen here before showing)

useEffect:
Render → UI Updates → User sees screen → useEffect runs
                     ↑                    ↑
              (Sees 0 for a moment)   (Then changes to 95)
              
 
 Example:
              
function Body() {
  const [kesa, setKesa] = useState(0)

  // ✅ useLayoutEffect - You CANNOT see 0 on screen
  useLayoutEffect(() => {      
    if (kesa === 0) {  
      setKesa(95)  // Changes BEFORE showing
    }
  }, [kesa])

  // ❌ useEffect - You CAN see 0 for a split second
  // useEffect(() => {      
  //   if (kesa === 0) {  
  //     setKesa(95)  // Changes AFTER showing
  //   }
  // }, [kesa])

  const changeKesa = () => {
    setKesa(0)
  }

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Test useeffect {kesa}</h1>
      <button onClick={changeKesa}>Change Kesa</button>
    </div>
  )
}

🔑 Key Takeaway
useLayoutEffect = Changes before user sees screen (no flicker)
useEffect = Changes after user sees screen (possible flicker)

 When to Use Which
Use useEffect (Most Common)	Use useLayoutEffect (Rare)
✅ Fetching data from API	✅ Measuring DOM elements (width, height)
✅ Setting up subscriptions	✅ Getting scroll position
✅ Adding event listeners	✅ Animations that need smooth start
✅ Updating document title	✅ Preventing visual flickers
✅ Logging/analytics	        ✅ Syncing with external DOM libraries


❌ Disadvantages of useEffect
#	Disadvantage	                          Explanation

1	Visual Flicker	                          User sees intermediate values briefly before final update
2	Layout Shift	                          Content can jump/move after user already sees it
3	Flash of Unstyled Content	          May see unstyled content before CSS loads
4	Inconsistent Measurements	          Getting element dimensions may be outdated
5	FOUC (Flash of Unstyled Content)	  User sees raw HTML before styles apply


❌ Disadvantages of useLayoutEffect
#	Disadvantage	                          Explanation

1	Blocks Painting	                          Browser cannot paint screen until it completes
2	Slower Performance	                  Makes app feel laggy/slow
3	Hurts User Experience	                  User sees delayed response
4	Can Cause Errors in SSR	                  Crashes in Next.js / Server-Side Rendering
5	Overkill for Most Cases	                  Using it unnecessarily hurts performance



📊 Comparison Table
Issue	         useEffect	                  useLayoutEffect

Flickering	✅ Has flicker	                  ❌ No flicker
Blocks Painting	❌ Doesn't block	          ✅ Blocks painting
Performance	✅ Good	                  ⚠️ Can be bad
SSR Compatible	✅ Yes                            ❌ Warning/Error
Measures DOM	❌ Inaccurate	                   ✅ Accurate

